{
  "name": "Rebuke of the Arbiter",
  "type": "ability",
  "img": "modules/titan-vttrpg-compendium/icons/paths/Arbiter_Path_Icon.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 1 Resolve</p><p><strong>Range:</strong> 30 spaces</p><p>You have learned to unravel supernatural abilities before or after they take effect.</p><p>When a creature you can see within <strong>30 spaces</strong> uses a <strong>Path</strong> ability, you can spend <strong>1 Resolve</strong> to disrupt the ability before it takes effect.</p><p>This requires a successful <strong>Counteract</strong> check using <strong>Soul (Metaphysics)</strong>. If the creature does not normally make a check to use their ability, they must make a <strong>4:1 Soul (Metaphysics)</strong> check to determine the <strong>Complexity</strong> of the <strong>Counteract</strong> check.</p><p>If you succeed, the ability is countered and has no effect. If you fail, the ability takes effect as normal.</p><p>Alternatively, you can attempt to remove the effect of a <strong>Path</strong> ability within <strong>30 spaces</strong>. If you succeed, the effect is removed. If you fail, and try to remove the effect again, the <strong>Complexity</strong> of the <strong>Counteract</strong> check increases by <strong>+1</strong>.</p>",
